       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily. A dose of 30 mg raises the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. In overdose it can also cause prolonged vasodilatory shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n1. **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **5 mg PO once daily**, a common starting or maintenance dose.\n3. **Another dose.** For example, you might have meant 3 mg or 3 \u00d7 10 mg, or you might have a specific reason for 30 mg.\n\nIf 30 mg is intentional, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
